From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:30:57 +0000
Subject: Judge top-level navigations by their own JIT setting

NavigationRequest::GetUrlInfo() passed the origin of the current main frame
as the top origin of every navigation. SiteInfo::Create() uses that origin
only to turn JIT on: a page with JIT allowed also allows JIT in its
subframes, and a page with JIT blocked does not take JIT away from a
subframe whose own setting allows it. For a main-frame navigation that
frame is the page being left. When JIT was allowed for one site, a link or
a popup from that site to another site therefore gave the new site's first
document a renderer with JIT, although JIT stayed blocked for it.

Pass the top origin only for subframe navigations. A main-frame navigation,
including the first navigation of a popup, is now decided by the JIT
setting of its destination. Subframes and PDF content behave as before.

